id: SCA-066
title: Hex or Unicode encoded shell commands
category: supply-chain
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .sh .bash .py .js .rb
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: (\\x[0-9a-fA-F]{2}){8,}
    message: Long hex escape sequence — attackers use hex encoding to obfuscate malicious commands like curl/wget.
  - regex: (\\u[0-9a-fA-F]{4}){6,}
    message: Long unicode escape sequence — used to obfuscate malicious commands and evade static analysis.
fix: Investigate long hex/unicode escape sequences. Decode and review the content. Legitimate uses (binary protocols) should be documented.
